y tools like you know  foreshadowing and how to you know how to  write prophecy compelling prophecy that  doesn't seem you know uh  dinky or foregone conclusion all these  things that i i still use today that i  learned from those books so it was just  really exciting for me to be able to  meet george and then we and then we hit  it off and then you know on down the  road we go you know some you know five  six seven years later it turned into a  job offer which still i mean as still it  still  blows my mind that i'm that i'm sitting  here doing the show during an interview  with ryan and george ryan more or less  said he has studied a song of ice and  fire and in doing so it helped him learn  how to write stories of his own when i  heard that it had me very excited for  house of the dragon because it really  does seem like they found the best man  for the job that is if you ask me near  the end of the video we also hear george  rr martin say he wanted ryan to write on  the show because he knew ryan knew his a  song of ice and fire novels better than  any of the other writers hbo originally  wanted on the show  a round of development  if you go back  when it was clear that the game of  thrones was ending that dave and dan  wanted to end it after seven seasons or  something  hbo started looking to develop other  other shows  and um the two that i pitched were  dancing with a dragon which became  uh house of dragon and uh  the dunkin egg thing  but there were a number of other shows  that were developed at that time  most of them put together by writers  that hbo hired  uh  who had never read my books  and who i guess had watched the show and  they were doing and when we were getting  into this i didn't want that anymore i  obviously none of those shows ultimately  got on the air i thought you know i want  people if they're going to be working in  my world i want them to actually have  read my books and i liked ryan's work  and i knew they knew the world he had  read t